[
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "# Operator panel (owner: Miguel)\n\nA LoTV panel, `RotaLivreOps` in the HUB (<http://localhost:3000>), for the team during the demo: how many barriers are\nactive per source, which ones, how many \"Já não está\" answers each has, and the state of the city alerts import.\nRead-only: it has no write controls (the city switch stays a retained publish, see `city_alerts.lotnb`).\n\n- **`access/ops/summary`** (retained, QoS 1, written only by the broker; topic map in `README.md`):\n  `{updated_at, active: {app, city, demo, total}, barriers: [{id, source, kind, description, expires_at, gone_count}],\n  feedback: [{barrier_id, gone_count, last_answered_at}]}`. `barriers` lists only active ones (not expired); `feedback`\n  lists every barrier with at least one stored answer, active or not. Source: `city-*` → city, `demo-*` → demo, any\n  other id → app.\n- `OpsSummary` (Python, tests in `services/tests/test_ops_summary.py`) is **not pure, on purpose** (agreed 24/10): it\n  keeps the barriers and answers in module memory under a lock. The broker runs an Action's triggers concurrently, so\n  read-change-publish on the retained summary lost updates (a city import burst counted 6 of 24). Module globals\n  persist between `CALL PYTHON` calls, and the lock makes each change exact (30 concurrent calls: 30/30). After a\n  restart or redeploy the module seeds itself from the retained summary (durability is on).\n- `OpsSummaryOnBarrier` (every `access/barriers/<id>` message: adds, updates, or drops an empty, unreadable or expired\n  one), `OpsSummaryOnFeedback` (on `access/feedback/<id>/last_answered_at`, which `StoreBarrierFeedback` publishes after\n  `gone_count`) and `OpsSummaryRefresh` (every 15 s: republishes, so barriers that expired in the meantime drop out and a summary\n  published out of order is corrected).\n- An Action only sees new messages: barriers retained before these Actions were deployed are not in the summary until\n  they are published again (`on`/`off` for the city ones, `barriers.py seed` for the demo ones)."
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "python",
    "value": "# Script Name: OpsSummary\n\"\"\"Operator summary of the barriers: active count per source, active barriers and \"gone\" answers.\n\nFunctions called from LoT take str arguments and return the whole summary as a JSON str (broker 2.22.0).\n\nNot pure, on purpose: the state lives in this module, under a lock. The broker runs an Action's triggers\nconcurrently, so reading the retained summary, changing it and publishing it back lost updates (6 of 24 barriers\ncounted on a city import burst, 24/10). The module persists between calls, so the lock makes every change exact.\nAfter a restart or a redeploy the state is empty and is seeded from the retained summary passed in.\nTwo publishes can still arrive out of order; OpsSummaryRefresh republishes every 15 s, which fixes that.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport re\nimport threading\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\nFRACTION = re.compile(r\"\\.(\\d{6})\\d+\")\nSAFE_ID = re.compile(r\"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}$\")\nSOURCES = (\"app\", \"city\", \"demo\")\nMAX_DESCRIPTION = 80\nLOCK = threading.Lock()\nSTATE = {}  # \"barriers\": {id: barrier}, \"feedback\": {barrier id: answer row}; empty until the first call\n\n\ndef _parse_time(text):\n    \"\"\"ISO 8601 to an aware UTC datetime, or None. Accepts Z and .NET's 7-digit fractions.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(text, str) or not text:\n        return None\n    text = FRACTION.sub(r\".\\1\", text.strip()).replace(\"Z\", \"+00:00\").replace(\"z\", \"+00:00\")\n    try:\n        moment = datetime.fromisoformat(text)\n    except ValueError:\n        return None\n    if moment.tzinfo is None:\n        moment = moment.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n    return moment.astimezone(timezone.utc)\n\n\ndef _iso(moment):\n    return moment.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.\") + f\"{moment.microsecond // 1000:03d}Z\"\n\n\ndef source_of(barrier_id):\n    \"\"\"city-* and demo-* are the broker's and the demo script's; everything else came from the app.\"\"\"\n    for prefix in (\"city\", \"demo\"):\n        if barrier_id.startswith(prefix + \"-\"):\n            return prefix\n    return \"app\"\n\n\ndef _load(summary_json):\n    try:\n        summary = json.loads(summary_json) if summary_json else {}\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        summary = {}\n    if not isinstance(summary, dict):\n        summary = {}\n    barriers = {b[\"id\"]: b for b in summary.get(\"barriers\") or [] if isinstance(b, dict) and \"id\" in b}\n    feedback = {f[\"barrier_id\"]: f for f in summary.get(\"feedback\") or []\n                if isinstance(f, dict) and \"barrier_id\" in f}\n    return barriers, feedback\n\n\ndef _dump(barriers, feedback, now_moment):\n    active = {}\n    for b_id, b in barriers.items():\n        expires = _parse_time(b.get(\"expires_at\"))\n        if expires is None or expires > now_moment:  # like the app: only a past expires_at hides a barrier\n            active[b_id] = b\n    rows = []\n    for b_id in sorted(active, key=lambda i: (SOURCES.index(active[i][\"source\"]), i)):\n        row = dict(active[b_id])\n        row[\"gone_count\"] = feedback.get(b_id, {}).get(\"gone_count\", 0)\n        rows.append(row)\n    counts = {source: sum(1 for b in active.values() if b[\"source\"] == source) for source in SOURCES}\n    counts[\"total\"] = len(active)\n    answers = sorted(feedback.values(), key=lambda f: (-f[\"gone_count\"], f[\"barrier_id\"]))\n    return json.dumps({\n        \"updated_at\": _iso(now_moment),\n        \"active\": counts,\n        \"barriers\": rows,\n        \"feedback\": answers,\n    }, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n\ndef _now(now):\n    return _parse_time(now) or datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n\n\ndef _state(summary_json):\n    \"\"\"The module's maps, seeded from the retained summary the first time (call with LOCK held).\"\"\"\n    if not STATE:\n        STATE[\"barriers\"], STATE[\"feedback\"] = _load(summary_json)\n    return STATE[\"barriers\"], STATE[\"feedback\"]\n\n\ndef reset():\n    \"\"\"Forget the in-memory state (tests; the next call seeds it again from the summary it gets).\"\"\"\n    with LOCK:\n        STATE.clear()\n    return \"{}\"\n\n\ndef apply_barrier(summary_json, barrier_id, payload, now):\n    \"\"\"A message on access/barriers/<id>: add or update it, or drop it when it is empty, unreadable or expired.\"\"\"\n    now_moment = _now(now)\n    barrier_id = str(barrier_id or \"\")\n    try:\n        report = json.loads(payload) if payload else None\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        report = None\n    ok = (isinstance(report, dict) and isinstance(report.get(\"lat\"), (int, float))\n          and isinstance(report.get(\"lon\"), (int, float)))  # the app ignores the same messages\n    expires = _parse_time(report.get(\"expires_at\")) if ok else None\n    with LOCK:\n        barriers, feedback = _state(summary_json)\n        if not SAFE_ID.match(barrier_id):\n            pass\n        elif not ok or (expires is not None and expires <= now_moment):\n            barriers.pop(barrier_id, None)\n        else:\n            description = \" \".join(str(report.get(\"description\") or \"\").split())\n            if len(description) > MAX_DESCRIPTION:\n                description = description[:MAX_DESCRIPTION - 1].rstrip() + \"…\"\n            barriers[barrier_id] = {\n                \"id\": barrier_id,\n                \"source\": source_of(barrier_id),\n                \"kind\": str(report.get(\"kind\") or \"other\"),\n                \"description\": description,\n                \"expires_at\": _iso(expires) if expires else \"\",\n            }\n        return _dump(barriers, feedback, now_moment)\n\n\ndef apply_feedback(summary_json, barrier_id, gone_count, last_answered_at, now):\n    \"\"\"A stored \"gone\" answer (access/feedback/<id>/...): record the barrier's count and latest answer time.\n\n    A count that is empty, non-numeric or 0 (the topics were cleared) removes the barrier from the list.\n    \"\"\"\n    now_moment = _now(now)\n    barrier_id = str(barrier_id or \"\")\n    try:\n        count = int(float(gone_count))\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        count = 0\n    with LOCK:\n        barriers, feedback = _state(summary_json)\n        if SAFE_ID.match(barrier_id):\n            if count > 0:\n                feedback[barrier_id] = {\"barrier_id\": barrier_id, \"gone_count\": count,\n                                        \"last_answered_at\": str(last_answered_at or \"\")}\n            else:\n                feedback.pop(barrier_id, None)\n        return _dump(barriers, feedback, now_moment)\n\n\ndef refresh(summary_json, now):\n    \"\"\"The summary at `now`: barriers that expired since the last message are no longer active (every 15 s).\"\"\"\n    now_moment = _now(now)\n    with LOCK:\n        barriers, feedback = _state(summary_json)\n        return _dump(barriers, feedback, now_moment)"
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE ACTION OpsSummaryOnBarrier\nON TOPIC \"access/barriers/+\" DO\n    SET \"barrier_id\" WITH TOPIC POSITION 3\n    SET \"body\" WITH PAYLOAD AS STRING\n    SET \"summary\" WITH GET TOPIC \"access/ops/summary\" AS STRING\n    SET \"now\" WITH TIMESTAMP \"ISO\"\n    CALL PYTHON \"OpsSummary.apply_barrier\"\n        WITH ({summary}, {barrier_id}, {body}, {now})\n        RETURN AS {next}\n    PUBLISH TOPIC \"access/ops/summary\" WITH {next} WITH RETAIN QOS1"
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE ACTION OpsSummaryOnFeedback\nON TOPIC \"access/feedback/+/last_answered_at\" DO\n    SET \"barrier_id\" WITH TOPIC POSITION 3\n    SET \"answered_at\" WITH PAYLOAD AS STRING\n    SET \"count\" WITH GET TOPIC \"access/feedback/\" + {barrier_id} + \"/gone_count\" AS STRING\n    SET \"summary\" WITH GET TOPIC \"access/ops/summary\" AS STRING\n    SET \"now\" WITH TIMESTAMP \"ISO\"\n    CALL PYTHON \"OpsSummary.apply_feedback\"\n        WITH ({summary}, {barrier_id}, {count}, {answered_at}, {now})\n        RETURN AS {next}\n    PUBLISH TOPIC \"access/ops/summary\" WITH {next} WITH RETAIN QOS1"
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE ACTION OpsSummaryRefresh\nON EVERY 15 SECONDS DO\n    SET \"summary\" WITH GET TOPIC \"access/ops/summary\" AS STRING\n    SET \"now\" WITH TIMESTAMP \"ISO\"\n    CALL PYTHON \"OpsSummary.refresh\"\n        WITH ({summary}, {now})\n        RETURN AS {next}\n    PUBLISH TOPIC \"access/ops/summary\" WITH {next} WITH RETAIN QOS1"
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE PANEL \"RotaLivreOps\"\n    WITH TITLE \"Rota Livre: barrier operations\"\n    WITH LAYOUT \"grid\" COLUMNS 4\n    WITH VISIBILITY PUBLIC\n    WITH STATE PUBLISHED\n\n    ADD COMPONENT \"AppBarriersGauge\" WITH TYPE \"gauge\"\n        SET LABEL \"Active app reports\"\n        SET UNIT \"barriers\"\n        SET RANGE FROM 0 TO 30\n        BIND VALUE TO TOPIC \"access/ops/summary\" WITH JSON_PATH \"active.app\" AS NUMBER\n\n    ADD COMPONENT \"CityBarriersGauge\" WITH TYPE \"gauge\"\n        SET LABEL \"Active city works (Câmara)\"\n        SET UNIT \"barriers\"\n        SET RANGE FROM 0 TO 50\n        BIND VALUE TO TOPIC \"access/ops/summary\" WITH JSON_PATH \"active.city\" AS NUMBER\n\n    ADD COMPONENT \"DemoBarriersGauge\" WITH TYPE \"gauge\"\n        SET LABEL \"Active demo barriers\"\n        SET UNIT \"barriers\"\n        SET RANGE FROM 0 TO 10\n        BIND VALUE TO TOPIC \"access/ops/summary\" WITH JSON_PATH \"active.demo\" AS NUMBER\n\n    ADD COMPONENT \"CityImportIndicator\" WITH TYPE \"indicator\"\n        SET LABEL \"City alerts import (on/off)\"\n        SET ON_VALUE \"on\" WITH COLOR \"#22c55e\"\n        SET ON_VALUE \"off\" WITH COLOR \"#94a3b8\"\n        BIND STATE TO TOPIC \"access/city/alerts/enabled\"\n\n    ADD COMPONENT \"ActiveBarriersTrend\" WITH TYPE \"realtime-chart\"\n        SET LABEL \"Active barriers\"\n        SET UNIT \"barriers\"\n        SET TRACE_DEPTH 120\n        SET Y_MIN 0\n        BIND VALUE TO TOPIC \"access/ops/summary\" WITH JSON_PATH \"active.total\" AS NUMBER\n            SET SERIES_LABEL \"All sources\"\n\n    ADD COMPONENT \"CityLastOkText\" WITH TYPE \"text\"\n        SET LABEL \"City import: last success (UTC)\"\n        BIND CONTENT TO TOPIC \"access/city/alerts/last_ok\"\n\n    ADD COMPONENT \"CityLastErrorText\" WITH TYPE \"text\"\n        SET LABEL \"City import: last failed fetch (UTC)\"\n        BIND CONTENT TO TOPIC \"access/city/alerts/last_error\"\n\n    ADD COMPONENT \"SummaryUpdatedText\" WITH TYPE \"text\"\n        SET LABEL \"Summary updated (UTC)\"\n        BIND CONTENT TO TOPIC \"access/ops/summary\" WITH JSON_PATH \"updated_at\"\n\n    ADD COMPONENT \"ActiveBarriersTable\" WITH TYPE \"table\" AT COLUMN 1 ROW 3 SPAN 4 COLUMNS\n        SET COLUMNS \"id,source,kind,description,expires_at,gone_count\"\n        SET COLUMN_LABELS \"Barrier,Source,Kind,Description,Expires,Gone answers\"\n        SET COLUMN_TYPES \"string,badge,badge,string,datetime,number\"\n        SET SORTABLE true\n        SET SEARCHABLE true\n        SET PAGE_SIZE 10\n        BIND DATA TO TOPIC \"access/ops/summary\" WITH JSON_PATH \"barriers\"\n\n    ADD COMPONENT \"GoneAnswersTable\" WITH TYPE \"table\" AT COLUMN 1 ROW 4 SPAN 4 COLUMNS\n        SET COLUMNS \"barrier_id,gone_count,last_answered_at\"\n        SET COLUMN_LABELS \"Barrier,Gone answers,Latest answer\"\n        SET COLUMN_TYPES \"string,number,datetime\"\n        SET SORTABLE true\n        SET PAGE_SIZE 10\n        BIND DATA TO TOPIC \"access/ops/summary\" WITH JSON_PATH \"feedback\""
  }
]
